{"items":[{"source_ids":["n1","n2"],"text":"# pi-identity
pi-identity provides scoped automatic attachment of living notebook notes and auditing. Following issue #612, commit 7a362d6, note headers support `paths:` and `touches:`. Path prefixes or globs scope automatic attachment when chats read, edit, grep, or run shell commands (including bash) against matching paths; touch triggers scope attachment when queued tasks start with matching touches. Configure scopes with `notebook(action="edit", id="<id>", paths=[...], touches=[...])`.

`notebook(action="audit")` checks note integrity. Reported issues can include dead disk or file paths, lines longer than 240 characters, empty `##` sections, and leftover `(n...)` or `(d...)` references. The clean result is `Audit OK: 0 issues`."}],"ejected":[]}

{"items":[{"source_ids":["n1","n2"],"text":"Contract: Answers 19 yes/no checks, alongside wt check, ui-check, and doc-check. Usage: `test-check <repo> [--level N] [--json] [--wt-config <file>] [--land-records <file>]`. Exit codes: 0 pass, 1 findings, 2 usage error or unreadable input. `--json` emits one object. QA's seam defines stable UPPER-KEBAB IDs and JSON shape; findings include ID, file[:line], a plain sentence and next step. Seam 2 JSON requires seam: 2 and per-check required; observed and human findings are bounded single lines.

Implementation: Ops builds on master and lands with wt land; QA owns the standard, seam, failing fixture acceptance tests and blind final check. The land gate is `node scripts/select-tests.mjs --for-check`. `bin/test-check` is a three-line Node shim calling `process.exit(runCli(process.argv.slice(2)))`; `lib/test-check/*.mjs` uses ESM/plain Node, files under 500 lines, and `lib/wt.mjs`'s wt.yaml reader. Builds/new dependencies require Ops approval. `node:test` tests live in `test/test-check-*.test.mjs`, discovered by npm test via `scripts/test.sh 'test/*.test.mjs'`; fixtures belong in `test/fixtures/test-check/`, never real repositories. Ops installs after landing: `ln -s /home/shinelay/projects/agent-tools/bin/test-check ~/.local/bin/test-check`. Require a README.md section and doc-check-clean `docs/test-check.md`.

Scanning: Hold at most one file's text at a time; handle 60,000 test files on Node's default heap. No network, model calls, writes into checked repositories or execution of their tests; identical input yields identical output. Seam 2 supports three-hop/argument-list runners, gitignore-aware scanning, current-config land records, release.files, linked worktrees, and fit helpers versus focused tests."}],"ejected":[]}

